# C++ Class and Object

## Description

This program demonstrates the basic concept of classes and objects in C++. A `Student` class is created to store a student's name and age. An object of the class is then created and used to display the student's details.

## Class Used

### 1. Student

The `Student` class contains two data members and one member function.

### Data Members

- `name` – Stores the student's name.
- `age` – Stores the student's age.

### Member Function

- `show()` – Displays the student's name and age.

## Main Function

The `main()` function creates an object named `s1` of the `Student` class.

The values `"Amit"` and `20` are assigned to the object's data members using the dot (`.`) operator.

The `show()` function is then called to display the details.

## Output

Amit 20

## OOP Concept Used

- Class
- Object
- Data Members
- Member Function
- Dot Operator

## Program Flow

Start
  ↓
Define Student Class
  ↓
Create Object s1
  ↓
Assign Name and Age
  ↓
Call show()
  ↓
Display Student Details
  ↓
End